  "answer": "Found the bug already — `add` subtracts instead of adding. Let me check the tests and how to run them.\nThe test uses `bun:test`. Fixing the one-line bug now:\nNow running the existing test suite:\nDone. ✅\n\n## Summary of the fix\n\n**Bug:** In `src/add.ts`, the `add` function returned `a - b` (subtraction) instead of `a + b`, so every addition result was wrong — e.g. `add(2, 3)` returned `-1` instead of `5`.\n\n**Fix:** A one-character change — replaced the subtraction operator with addition:\n\n```ts\nexport function add(a: number, b: number) { return a + b }\n```\n\n**Verification:** `bun test` passes — 1 test, 5 assertions across signed inputs (positive, negative, zero) all green:\n\n```\n(pass) addition across signed inputs\n 1 pass, 0 fail\n```\n\n**Preserved:** The public signature `(a: number, b: number)` is unchanged, `test/oracle.test.ts`, `package.json`, and `AGENTS.md` were not touched."
